# The V7 spec is a delivered artefact, not source we edit. Git's automatic
# line-ending conversion would rewrite it on checkout, so the working copy would
# no longer be byte-identical to what the client sent — and
# tests/unit/spec-freshness.test.ts compares exactly those bytes. `-text`
# disables the conversion in both directions and stores it verbatim.
spec/v7/*.html -text

# The delivery folder itself, now tracked rather than living only on the machine
# it was delivered to. It is the other half of that same byte comparison, so it
# needs the same treatment: without this git stores it normalised and hands back
# CRLF on checkout, while spec/v7 stays verbatim, and the two stop matching on
# any machine that is not this one.
"client requirements/**" -text
